      "format": "shorts",
      "language": "en",
      "title": "All 10 Korean vowels in one song! 아 야 어 여 오 요 우 유 으 이 #learnkorean",
      "text": "Sing and move along with Mongle — one song, all 10 basic Korean vowels (Hangul).\n\nEach vowel's short stroke points the way your arms go:\n아 (a) → right · 어 (eo) → left · 오 (o) → up · 우 (u) → down\n으 (eu) → stretch out wide · 이 (i) → stand straight\nTwo short strokes = do it twice: 야 (ya) · 여 (yeo) · 요 (yo) · 유 (yu)\n\nRomanization appears under every letter, and English captions (CC) have the lyrics.\n\nAt the end, try reading 아이 · 오이 · 우유 before you hear them!\n\nHangul for Beginners · 한글 초보단계 #1 — made for Hangul Day 2026 (Oct 9).\nSYNK LAB · learn Korean the fun way, with Mongle.\n#learnkorean #hangul #koreanvowels",
      "alt": [
        "A felt kid and the coral felt mascot Mongle dance the Korean vowels ㅏ ㅓ ㅗ ㅜ ㅡ ㅣ, drawn in blue, under a white card reading “All 10 Korean vowels in one song!”"
